# Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and FILL IN: copying it blank is worse than not having it at all. Read by the Cloudflare Vite
# plugin / `wrangler dev`.
#
# An empty `KEY=` line is a DEFINED empty string, not an absent value, so it shadows whatever `shopify app dev` injects. That is why
# SHOPIFY_API_SECRET is not listed below: `npm run dev` injects it (with SHOPIFY_API_KEY, SCOPES and the tunnel URL).
#
# Secret NAMES are declared in wrangler.jsonc (`secrets.required`), so `wrangler types` does not need this file: a fresh clone compiles
# with no `.dev.vars` at all.

# Signs the links of support attachments. Any long random string locally.
ATTACHMENT_TOKEN_SECRET=dev-attachment-secret

# The HMAC key every app and the portal hash events with. Locally anything; production uses the shared secret and EVENT_HASH_KEY_ID.
EVENT_HASH_SECRET=dev-event-hash-secret

# Partner API token (reads this app's subscription). Empty = the subscription refresh reports `not_configured` and the shop stays on the
# free plan. Needs PARTNER_ORG_ID and PARTNER_APP_ID (vars in wrangler.jsonc; the Partner Dashboard URL and the app overview).
# PARTNER_API_TOKEN=

# Optional: Cloudflare Turnstile secret for the public support form (the site key is TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY in wrangler.jsonc). Empty = check off.
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Optional: custom shop domains Shopify may authenticate (a comma list is not supported: one domain).
# SHOP_CUSTOM_DOMAIN=

# Transactional email. The `send_email` binding is declared, but nothing sends until the domain is onboarded and EMAIL_FROM is set (in
# wrangler.jsonc vars, per environment: it is not a secret):
#   npx wrangler email sending enable yourdomain.com
# The binding is `remote: true`, so a send during `npm run dev` goes through the REAL service and needs `wrangler login`.

# NOTE: never set SHOPIFY_APP_URL here: it would shadow the live tunnel URL that `shopify app dev` injects.

# The App Store listing handle (apps.shopify.com/<handle>). Leave it unset locally and before the app is listed: the landing page then
# shows the shop-domain install form. Setting it makes every Install button link to the listing and hides the form.
# SHOPIFY_APP_HANDLE=
